# ── Supabase (required for cloud sync + auth) ─────────────────────────────────
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then copy these from:
#   Project Settings → API → Project URL / anon public key
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# ── Usage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Copy this file to .env  (already in .gitignore)
# 2. Fill in your Supabase project URL and anon key
# 3. Run the SQL in CLOUD_SYNC_PLAN.md §7.1 in your Supabase SQL editor
# 4. npm run dev (or npm run tauri dev)
#
# The anon key is safe to commit in principle (RLS protects all data),
# but we keep it in .env to avoid accidental exposure.
